Fixes "setup:di:compile" failing on macOS (Docker Desktop) with
"RecursiveDirectoryIterator::__construct(.../vendor/aheadworks/module-reward-points/Plugin/PayPal): Failed to open directory: No such file or directory".

Root cause: OrderAdapterPlugin lives in Plugin/PayPal/ and is registered in etc/di.xml as Plugin\PayPal\...,
but declares the namespace Plugin\Paypal\..., which is not PSR-4 compliant. During compilation Magento's ClassesScanner
calls class_exists() with the declared name, so Composer's PSR-4 autoloader looks up Plugin/Paypal/... . On the
case-insensitive macOS filesystem shared into the container this lookup succeeds and the Linux guest caches the
directory under the name "Paypal". The DirectoryScanner of the "Application code generator" step then opens
Plugin/PayPal and gets ENOENT. On case-sensitive filesystems (CI, production) the wrong lookup simply misses, which is why
the bug does not show up there.
Fix: declare the namespace with the same case as the directory and di.xml.

diff --git a/Plugin/PayPal/Braintree/Gateway/Data/Order/OrderAdapterPlugin.php b/Plugin/PayPal/Braintree/Gateway/Data/Order/OrderAdapterPlugin.php
index 6cbd61f..2ec988a 100644
--- a/Plugin/PayPal/Braintree/Gateway/Data/Order/OrderAdapterPlugin.php
+++ b/Plugin/PayPal/Braintree/Gateway/Data/Order/OrderAdapterPlugin.php
@@ -1,7 +1,10 @@
 <?php
 declare(strict_types=1);

-namespace Aheadworks\RewardPoints\Plugin\Paypal\Braintree\Gateway\Data\Order;
+// BEGIN PATCH
+// namespace Aheadworks\RewardPoints\Plugin\Paypal\Braintree\Gateway\Data\Order;
+namespace Aheadworks\RewardPoints\Plugin\PayPal\Braintree\Gateway\Data\Order;
+// END PATCH

 use Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException;
 use PayPal\Braintree\Gateway\Data\Order\OrderAdapter as Subject;
